`ModuleRunner` logs full-reload errors through its `logger` option (a `Logger`-shaped object with `error`/`warn`/`info`/`debug`/`clearScreen`/`hasErrorLogged`). A framework can pass a custom logger when constructing the runner, or override the `logger.error` method to filter/suppress those messages. There's no dedicated flag to disable only full-reload error logging, so interception is the practical approach.

```ts
const runner = new ModuleRunner(transport, {
  logger: {
    ...defaultLogger,
    error(msg, opts) {
      if (isFullReloadError(msg)) return; // suppress
      defaultLogger.error(msg, opts);
    },
  },
});
```

If you need finer control, check the `ModuleRunner` source for the exact message/`opts` shape used on full reload, since it isn't a stable public API. I'm not certain of a documented, supported toggle beyond the logger.

