This is a classic module-evaluation-order problem: lazy loading defers the module's top-level code until the dynamic `import()` resolves, so any global it sets up (e.g. `window.Prism`, `window.hljs`, or a Lexical global) doesn't exist yet when your code that depends on it runs. If your code reads the global synchronously at startup, it sees `undefined` because the lazy chunk hasn't executed. The fix is to `await` the import before touching the global, or to access it inside the resolved callback:

```js
