```

Then guard code with `if (__DEV__) { ... }` or `if (__FEATURE_X__) { ... }`. Vite/Rollup (and esbuild) will replace the identifier with the literal and drop the dead branch, provided the code is side-effect-free and the module is otherwise tree-shakeable. Avoid patterns like `const flag = someRuntimeValue` or dynamic property access, which defeat static analysis. Also ensure `"sideEffects": false` in your package.json if you're publishing a library.

